WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:13.099
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the fifth, November. Can you hear me all right? Teams is showing me two microphones, which feels excessive.</v>

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:21.269
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, you're fine. Anyone got weekend plans that don't involve getting absolutely soaked? Forecast looks lovely, if you're a duck.</v>

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:29.149
<v Tomasz Nowak>We were going walking. Apparently we're still going walking, whatever the weather. This wasn't my decision.</v>

00:00:29.989 --> 00:00:33.140
<v Jamie Brennan>Strong procurement process there. No consultation, order already placed.</v>

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we lose the whole morning to waterproof trousers. Closed stuff first?</v>

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:46.700
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I already swapped the filter on the Stretch Wrapper yesterday. That's finished, not another one for today.</v>

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:52.609
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Han. That was still sitting on the old view.</v>

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.500
<v Callum Reid>Same sort of thing here. I signed off the inspection on the line 2 robot on Tuesday. Done and closed.</v>

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:07.859
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the gas turbine two on Tuesday. That one's closed as well.</v>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.900
<v Fiona Doyle>Good. Old view makes it look like we've all been sitting about eating biscuits.</v>

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:21.400
<v Hannah Price>One observation, while I'm on. I noticed the IM1 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.200
<v Aisha Begum>Settled back, rather than staying up there?</v>

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.859
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, settled. Just passing that on, not raising any new work from it.</v>

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:40.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. We do need the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 hydraulics. That's the safety one.</v>

00:01:42.819 --> 00:01:49.469
<v Hannah Price>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 hydraulics by 11am. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:54.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Han. Yours, straight away, signed off by 11am.</v>

00:01:54.939 --> 00:02:01.590
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, no treating the paperwork like it's separate from the isolation. That's where people get themselves in a muddle.</v>

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.650
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. The sign-off is what I'm taking, not just a quick look and a tick.</v>

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. What else have we got on maintenance?</v>

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:19.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll check the guarding on the IM3 by end of day. Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:24.419
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomasz Nowak against the IM3 guarding, then. End of day, normal priority?</v>

00:02:25.419 --> 00:02:29.620
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, that's mine. No need to bump it above the safety-critical sign-off.</v>

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:37.330
<v Jamie Brennan>Stores blocker before we get onto the other kit: the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Forklift Fleet.</v>

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.590
<v Callum Reid>Right, so that's still a delivery blocker, not something we've actually got in the yard.</v>

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:51.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Still blocked. Just status, not promising a delivery or taking another chase out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:52.259 --> 00:03:01.009
<v Callum Reid>Separate from that, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Forklift Fleet. It's urgent. The due date on that is on the 3rd.</v>

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:10.349
<v Fiona Doyle>Which has gone, just to be clear. We're on the fifth. That's an overdue date, not a new future slot?</v>

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.860
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, overdue. Keep it as on the 3rd; I'm not quietly moving the deadline. I'll take the update.</v>

00:03:19.479 --> 00:03:25.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Cal. Urgent risk assessment update with you. The supplier hold doesn't turn that into cancelled work.</v>

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:33.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you also recalibrate the sensors on the line 1 TCU? Due on the 3rd, and drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.599
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 1 TCU. I'll take that.</v>

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:42.250
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, talking over you—same overdue position on that date?</v>

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:49.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. Due on the 3rd, already overdue. No date reset. Drop everything for that one, Callum.</v>

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:57.620
<v Callum Reid>Understood. The line 1 TCU comes first for me, then the urgent risk assessment. Both accepted.</v>

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:05.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you go to Harbour Road Warehouse to pick up the replacement parts for the water booster? Fairly important.</v>

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:12.319
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll do that. Harbour Road Warehouse for the water booster replacement parts.</v>

00:04:13.259 --> 00:04:18.509
<v Jamie Brennan>And that's separate from the Forklift Fleet delivery issue, before those two get mixed together.</v>

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.670
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, understood. I'm taking the collection from Harbour Road Warehouse, not the blocked supplier delivery.</v>

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Thanks, Aisha. Fairly important, that collection.</v>

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.720
<v Fiona Doyle>What about the contractor booking? Is that still in this lot?</v>

00:04:38.379 --> 00:04:44.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll book a contractor to look at the HV switchboard by Wednesday. No rush on that one.</v>

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:52.420
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah Okafor for that. And Wednesday is the booking deadline, not saying the contractor's physically there by then?</v>

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:58.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. I'll get the contractor booked by Wednesday. No rush; we're not inventing an attendance date.</v>

00:05:00.959 --> 00:05:05.509
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. Otherwise the diary suddenly contains a bloke who doesn't know he's coming.</v>

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:12.009
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll take vibration readings on the feedwater pump today at 2pm. That's fairly important.</v>

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:20.019
<v Fiona Doyle>So Sarah Okafor on the feedwater pump readings, today at 2pm. Not just sometime this afternoon.</v>

00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:24.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, today at 2pm. I'll take them.</v>

00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:30.079
<v Aisha Begum>Actual readings rather than the traditional hand-on-the-casing and 'seems a bit lively', then.</v>

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:35.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Preferably, yeah. Fairly important to have numbers rather than my highly scientific impression.</v>

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz Nowak, can you run a function test on the fire alarm panel Monday?</v>

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:51.579
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, no, I can't take Monday. I haven't got the capacity for that one. Don't put it against me.</v>

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:58.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, I'll take it instead. I'll run a function test on the fire alarm panel Monday.</v>

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:04.959
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, handed over to Sarah, not Tomasz Nowak. Monday stays as it was.</v>

00:06:06.069 --> 00:06:08.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Sarah for that one. Monday, accepted.</v>

00:06:10.399 --> 00:06:14.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything crossed over there? Particularly between actual actions and the old closed items.</v>

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:23.120
<v Jamie Brennan>Only to underline that the supplier confirmation is still a blocker. Nobody's taken a new stores action from that update.</v>

00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:28.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's how I've heard it. Status only.</v>

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:36.519
<v Hannah Price>And the Stretch Wrapper filter is definitely done. Please don't let the old entry breed another one.</v>

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:43.370
<v Callum Reid>Same for the line 2 robot inspection. Tuesday's sign-off stands; no repeat inspection agreed.</v>

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.149
<v Fiona Doyle>Lovely. Less duplication, more chance of escaping into the weekend rain.</v>

00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:56.240
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'm hoping the weather gets so bad the walk becomes a pub lunch. That's my entire weekend strategy.</v>

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:02.089
<v Aisha Begum>Very robust. Lots of contingency, absolutely no influence over the outcome.</v>

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.250
<v Callum Reid>Sounds familiar, that.</v>

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:12.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cheers, everyone. We've got the owners clear and the overdue dates haven't been hidden. Leave it there.</v>
